      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "It is generally believed that the Palmaz-Schatz stent maintains a strong radial force, preventing stent recoil. However, the capacity to prevent recoil is largely governed by the hardness or resistance of the lesion. We report two cases of \"acute Palmaz-Schatz stent recoil,\" documented by intravascular ultrasound, and suggest a novel treatment of this unusual problem."},
